        "original_id": "a6dc4950-c836-5ed7-969e-f4b4b75eab33",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mack Brown\n- Organizations: Texas Longhorns, Iowa State Cyclones, Kansas State Wildcats, Baylor Bears\n- Places: Darrell K Royal–Texas Memorial Stadium, Manhattan, Kansas\n- Events: 2011 college football season, Farmageddon series/showdown\n- Roles: head coach, college football commentator\n\nFacts:\n- In 2011, the Texas Longhorns football team was led by 14th-year head coach Mack Brown.\n- In 2011, the Texas Longhorns played their home games at Darrell K Royal–Texas Memorial Stadium.\n- In 2011, Iowa State began conference play with a home loss to the Texas Longhorns.\n- In 2011, Iowa State finished conference play with a loss in Manhattan, Kansas to the Kansas State Wildcats in the Farmageddon series and had a 3–6 conference record.\n- In 2011, Kansas State won all three non-conference games against Eastern Kentucky, Kent State, and Miami.\n- In 2011, Kansas State opened conference play with a close home victory over the Baylor Bears.\n- In 2011, Kansas State ended its conference schedule with a victory over rival Iowa State in the Farmageddon showdown.\n- Mack Brown is currently a college football commentator for ESPN.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
